# 26 - Bronze → Silver ETL Pipeline (Delta Practical) (Real Project)

This practical covers a real pipeline pattern:
- ingest → clean → transform → load
- bronze layer (raw)
- silver layer (clean)
- schema enforcement
- audit columns
- idempotency idea
- incremental batch concept

This is a real Data Engineering project pattern.

---

## 0) Architecture (Bronze-Silver)

### Bronze Layer
- raw ingestion
- minimal transformation
- schema may be loose
- keeps source truth

### Silver Layer
- cleaned and standardized
- correct schema
- null handling
- business ready

---

## 1) Create Sample Raw Data (Bronze)

```python
from pyspark.sql.functions import col, current_timestamp, trim, upper, coalesce, lit, to_date

raw_data = [
    (1, "  pramod  ", "it", "2026-02-01", "50000"),
    (2, "akash", "hr", "2026-02-02", None),
    (3, None, "it", "2026-02-03", "45000"),
    (4, "neha", None, None, "70000")
]

raw_df = spark.createDataFrame(raw_data, ["id", "name", "dept", "join_date", "salary"])
raw_df.show(truncate=False)
```

---

## 2) Write Bronze Delta Table

```python
bronze_path = "/tmp/delta/bronze/employees"

raw_df.write.format("delta")     .mode("overwrite")     .save(bronze_path)
```

---

## 3) Read Bronze

```python
bronze_df = spark.read.format("delta").load(bronze_path)
bronze_df.show(truncate=False)
```

---

## 4) Clean + Transform for Silver

Silver rules:
- trim + uppercase name
- dept uppercase
- join_date convert to date
- salary cast to int
- null handling
- add audit columns

```python
silver_df = bronze_df     .withColumn("name", upper(trim(coalesce(col("name"), lit("UNKNOWN")))))     .withColumn("dept", upper(trim(coalesce(col("dept"), lit("UNKNOWN")))))     .withColumn("join_date", to_date(col("join_date")))     .withColumn("salary", coalesce(col("salary").cast("int"), lit(0)))     .withColumn("created_at", current_timestamp())     .withColumn("updated_at", current_timestamp())

silver_df.show(truncate=False)
silver_df.printSchema()
```

---

## 5) Write Silver Delta Table

```python
silver_path = "/tmp/delta/silver/employees"

silver_df.write.format("delta")     .mode("overwrite")     .save(silver_path)
```

---

## 6) Validate Silver Output

```python
spark.read.format("delta").load(silver_path).show(truncate=False)
```

---

## 7) Best Practices

✅ Bronze should keep raw data  
✅ Silver should apply data quality rules  
✅ Add audit columns in silver  
✅ Use Delta for both layers  
✅ Use MERGE for incremental loads (next practicals)  

---

## 8) Summary

- Bronze = raw ingestion
- Silver = clean standardized layer
- Delta format is used in Databricks
- This is real DE pipeline design

